        "original_id": "73c686a4-b614-5dce-88b4-31f8e14c52d4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patty Smith Hill, Mildred Hill\n- Songs: \"Happy Birthday to You\", \"For He's a Jolly Good Fellow\"\n- Topics: Guinness World Records, song translations\n\nFacts:\n- Patty Smith Hill was born on March 27, 1868, and died on May 25, 1946.\n- Patty Smith Hill was a composer and teacher.\n- Patty Smith Hill and her sister Mildred Hill co-wrote the tune that later became popular as \"Happy Birthday to You\".\n- According to the 1998 Guinness World Records, \"Happy Birthday to You\" is the most recognized song in the English language.\n- According to the 1998 Guinness World Records, \"For He's a Jolly Good Fellow\" is the second most recognized song in the English language after \"Happy Birthday to You\".\n- The base lyrics of \"Happy Birthday to You\" have been translated into at least 18 languages.",
